Give the explicit mean-field Hamiltonian obtained after the decoupling:
\begin{aligned}
\hat{H}= & \sum_{i}\left(\varepsilon_{0}^{e}+\sum_{j} U_{i j}\langle n\rangle_{j}^{h}\right) \hat{n}_{i}^{e}+\sum_{i}\left(\varepsilon_{0}^{h}+\sum_{j} U_{i j}\langle n\rangle_{j}^{e}\right) \hat{n}_{i}^{h} \\
& +\sum_{i j}\left(t_{i j}^{e} \hat{a}_{i}^{e \dagger}+t_{i j}^{h} \hat{a}_{i}^{h \dagger}\right)-\sum_{i j} U_{i j}\langle n\rangle_{i}^{e}\langle n\rangle_{j}^{h},
\end{aligned}
treating the Hartree interaction of the opposite carrier species as a renormalization of the on-site energies and noting that the resulting single-particle Hamiltonian must be diagonalized iteratively until the local densities $\langle n\rangle_i^{\alpha}$ converge. [23]
